NiTTY — source README
=====================

NiTTY is a fork of PuTTY with a refreshed Windows UI and extra
session/window features. For an overview, credits (PuTTY and KiTTY),
and GitHub-oriented documentation, see README.md in this directory.

Building uses CMake. From the source root:

  cmake -S . -B build
  cmake --build build --config Release

On Windows with MSVC, ensure the compiler is on your PATH (e.g. run
the appropriate vcvars script), then use the same commands.

To install on Linux or macOS:

  cmake --build build --target install

On Unix, pterm may need setuid/setgid if you want it to record logins
in utmp/wtmp; the install step does not set that up—see upstream PuTTY
docs.

Documentation in various formats is built from the Halibut (.but) files
in doc/:

  https://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/halibut/

PuTTY’s home page (upstream):

  https://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/putty/

See LICENCE for licence conditions (inherited from PuTTY).
